{"name":"Halation","hex":"#d1d1ce","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"halation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The action of light surrounding some object as if making a halo.","The blurring of light around a bright area of a photographic image, or on a television screen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anti-halation backing","blocks":[{"text":"An anti-halation backing is a layer found in many photographic films—and almost all film intended for motion picture cameras—usually a coating on the back of the film base, though it is sometimes incorporated between the light-sensitive emulsion and the base. Its purpose is to absorb light that passes through the emulsion, thus preventing any light from being reflected back through the emulsion from the rear surface of the base, or from anything behind the film, such as the pressure plate of the camera. This prevents a halo-like effect (halation) from forming around bright points or edges in the image."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Halation-Effect.png/330px-Halation-Effect.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-halation_backing","wikidata":"Q4774373"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/01/Halation-before-after-simulation-digital-imitation-film-highlight-rolloff.jpg/500px-Halation-before-after-simulation-digital-imitation-film-highlight-rolloff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/01/Halation-before-after-simulation-digital-imitation-film-highlight-rolloff.jpg/500px-Halation-before-after-simulation-digital-imitation-film-highlight-rolloff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Digital \"halation\" before and after, to illustrate what an image looks like without and with halation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalation-before-after-simulation-digital-imitation-film-highlight-rolloff.jpg"}],"sounds":{"halation":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-halation.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/21/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-halation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-halation.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/21/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-halation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-halation.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.68875},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.62875},{"title":"Hale, Lighthouse Road - geograph.org.uk - 5323674","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Hale%2C_Lighthouse_Road_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5323674.jpg/500px-Hale%2C_Lighthouse_Road_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5323674.jpg","ratio":1.3278008298755186,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hale,_Lighthouse_Road_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5323674.jpg","share":0.23875},{"title":"Farmland near Hale - geograph.org.uk - 2864501","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Farmland_near_Hale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2864501.jpg/500px-Farmland_near_Hale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_286450